     1	"""HARN-2 — the browser product-harness oracles.
     2	
     3	These eight zero-opinion oracles judge the REAL product path (not just that the
     4	engine wrote files) over the browser evidence HARN-1b captures into a single
     5	``product_evidence`` dict. Each oracle reads its own slice; when the slice is absent
     6	(a headless run, or HARN-1b not yet wired) it SKIPS — so these never affect headless
     7	classification until a product-harness run supplies the evidence.
     8	
     9	product_evidence (the HARN-1b dossier, all keys optional):
    10	    {
    11	      "browser_ws":   {"connections": int, "closes": [{"code": int, "reason": str}]},
    12	      "lifecycle":    {"statuses": ["RUNNING", ...], "terminal": "FINISHED"|...},
    13	      "sidecar":      {"stopped_at_terminal": bool, "provider_calls_after_terminal": int},
    14	      "preview":      {"owner": "platform"|"model", "manual_port": bool,
    15	                       "shown_to_user": bool, "url": str},
    16	      "shown":        {"artifact_shown": bool, "preview_shown": bool},
    17	      "verification": {"ready_for_verification_called": bool, "passed": bool},
