   113	# Original ask_user description follows.
   114	_ASK_USER_DESCRIPTION = (
   115	    "Pause the run and ask the human user for input. Call this tool when YOU "
   116	    "(in your own reasoning) decide that the next step depends on human "
   117	    "judgment, a clarification, or a choice between options you can't pick "
   118	    "with confidence. Typical situations: you've tried 2-3 substantively "
   119	    "different approaches and they all failed; the right path depends on a "
   120	    "preference the user hasn't stated; an action would be irreversible and "
   121	    "you want confirmation of intent (not safety — that's the risk gate). "
   122	    "Provide a clear one-sentence `question` summarizing what you need. "
   123	    "Optionally, provide an `options` list of 2-3 concrete next-step "
   124	    "alternatives the user can click; each option must have a short "
   125	    "`title`, a brief `description`, and a `tool_name` + `arguments` shape "
   126	    "for the action that will run if the user picks it. Without options, "
